From 1f154e967833edd378a880d27dc843b476eebe39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: boxdot <dimitri@phnx.im>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:33:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(app): send keep-alives on idle listen streams  (#1649)

L7 proxies (UpCloud LB, Envoy) close streams without data after their
idle timeout, 120s on the UpCloud LB. HTTP/2 PINGs don't count, they
only keep the connection to the nearest proxy alive.

Clients now send a KeepAlive request on the QS and username listen
streams after 30s without other request. The server ignores it.

Listen handlers on the server also ignore empty requests now, so a
request variant unknown to the server no longer aborts the stream.
